WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.937
Welcome to Projectile Motion.

2
00:00:02.887 --> 00:00:19.175
Today we master the Maximum Height formula: H max equals v naught squared sine squared theta divided by two g. Pay close attention: the launch angle theta must always be measured relative to the horizontal, never the vertical axis.

3
00:00:19.175 --> 00:00:27.675
In NEET, common distractors provide the angle with the vertical, which traps students into confusing sine and cosine.

4
00:00:27.675 --> 00:00:31.300
Lock this core relationship into your memory.
